{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# MedGuard - Week 2: Fine-tune DeBERTa-v3 on leak-free splits\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook trains the interaction relation classifier on the **leak-free\n",
    "`pairwise` split**, applies **temperature scaling** on validation, and\n",
    "evaluates on the held-out test set with **calibration + selective\n",
    "prediction**.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Colab:** Runtime → Change runtime type → **T4 GPU**. `pip install\n",
    "> -e \".[ml]\"` then run all.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 0. Install + data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install -q -e \".[ml]\" 2>&1 | tail -3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import logging, json, numpy as np, pandas as pd\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "\n",
    "logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n",
    "\n",
    "from medguard.config import get_settings\n",
    "from medguard.data.splits import SplitStrategy, make_splits\n",
    "from medguard.evaluation.calibration import TemperatureScaler, compare_calibrators\n",
    "from medguard.evaluation.metrics import (\n",
    "    calibration_metrics,\n",
    "    classification_metrics,\n",
    "    selective_risk_coverage,\n"
    ")\n",
    "from medguard.modeling.classifier import CalibratedInteractionClassifier\n",
    "\n",
    "settings = get_settings(); settings.ensure_dirs()\n",
    "device = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n",
    "print(f\"Device: {device}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load data + leak-free splits\n",
    "\n",
    "We use the **pairwise** split (no drug pair crosses the boundary). If you\n",
    "want the harder cold-start evaluation, restrict the corpus to one\n",
    "therapeutic class first."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "INTERACTIONS = settings.processed_data_dir / \"interactions.parquet\"\n",
    "if not INTERACTIONS.exists():\n",
    "    INTERACTIONS = settings.processed_data_dir / \"demo_interactions.parquet\"\n",
    "    print(f\"Using demo KB: {INTERACTIONS}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_parquet(INTERACTIONS)\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(df)} interactions, {len(set(df.drug_a)|set(df.drug_b))} drugs\")\n",
    "\n",
    "train, val, test, report = make_splits(\n",
    "    df, strategy=SplitStrategy.PAIRWISE, seed=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(report.summary())\n",
    "print(f\"Train: {len(train)}, Val: {len(val)}, Test: {len(test)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Build labelled dataset (positives from KB, negatives sampled)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from medguard.modeling.baseline import DrugPairTfidfBaseline, build_baseline_df\n",
    "\n",
    "all_drugs = sorted({str(d) for d in df[\"drug_a\"]} | {str(d) for d in df[\"drug_b\"]})\n",
    "negatives = [\n",
    "    (all_drugs[i], all_drugs[j])\n",
    "    for i in range(len(all_drugs))\n",
    "    for j in range(i + 1, len(all_drugs))\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "train_df = build_baseline_df(train, negatives, n_negatives=len(train) * 2)\n",
    "val_df = build_baseline_df(val, negatives, n_negatives=len(val) * 2)\n",
    "test_df = build_baseline_df(test, negatives, n_negatives=len(test) * 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, frame in [(\"train\", train_df), (\"val\", val_df), (\"test\", test_df)]:\n",
    "    pos = int(frame[\"label\"].sum())\n",
    "    print(f\"{name}: {len(frame)} rows, {pos} positive, {len(frame)-pos} negative\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Train DeBERTa-v3\n",
    "\n",
    "We use `microsoft/deberta-v3-base` (86M params, MIT licence). On a Colab\n",
    "T4 this takes ~8-12 minutes for 3 epochs with bf16."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model = CalibratedInteractionClassifier(\n",
    "    encoder_name=\"microsoft/deberta-v3-base\",\n",
    "    threshold=0.5,\n",
    "    abstain_threshold=0.55,\n",
    "    max_length=128,\n",
    "    batch_size=32,\n",
    "    learning_rate=2e-5,\n",
    "    num_epochs=3,\n",
    "    warmup_ratio=0.1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model.train(train_df, val_df, output_dir=settings.artifacts_path / \"deberta_v3\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Calibrator T = {model.calibrator.temperature:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Calibration study\n",
    "\n",
    "Compare uncalibrated vs temperature vs Platt vs isotonic on validation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "test_pairs = list(zip(test_df[\"drug_a\"], test_df[\"drug_b\"], strict=False))\n",
    "y_true = test_df[\"label\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "\n",
    "test_logits = model.predict_logits(test_pairs)\n",
    "binary_logits = test_logits[:, 1] - test_logits[:, 0]\n",
    "\n",
    "calib_comparison = compare_calibrators(binary_logits, y_true, n_bins=15)\n",
    "print(json.dumps(calib_comparison, indent=2))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Full test evaluation with calibration + selective prediction"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "probs = model.calibrator.predict_proba(binary_logits)\n",
    "preds = (probs >= 0.5).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "metrics = classification_metrics(y_true, preds, y_score=probs)\n",
    "calib = calibration_metrics(y_true, probs)\n",
    "curve = selective_risk_coverage(y_true, probs)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Classification ===\")\n",
    "print(json.dumps(metrics.to_dict(), indent=2))\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Calibration ===\")\n",
    "print(json.dumps(calib.to_dict(), indent=2))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Risk-Coverage (every 5th point) ===\")\n",
    "for row in curve[::5]:\n",
    "    print(f\"  thresh={row['threshold']:.2f}  cov={row['coverage']:.2f}  risk={row['risk']:.3f}  n={row['n_kept']}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Leakage impact — your headline figure\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the same model on a naive random split vs the leak-free pairwise\n",
    "split. The F1 drop is the headline number."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from medguard.evaluation.metrics import leakage_impact\n",
    "\n",
    "def train_and_predict(split_name, train_data, test_data):\n",
    "    clf = CalibratedInteractionClassifier(\n",
    "        encoder_name=\"microsoft/deberta-v3-base\",\n",
    "        num_epochs=2,  # shorter for the leakage experiment\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    clf.train(train_data, val_df, output_dir=settings.artifacts_path / f\"deberta_leak_{split_name}\")\n",
    "    test_pairs = list(zip(test_data[\"drug_a\"], test_data[\"drug_b\"], strict=False))\n",
    "    y_true = np.ones(len(test_pairs))\n",
    "    y_pred = clf.predict(test_pairs)\n",
    "    return y_true, y_pred\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Training on random split...\")\n",
    "train_rand, val_rand, test_rand, _ = make_splits(df, strategy=SplitStrategy.RANDOM, seed=42)\n",
    "train_rand_df = build_baseline_df(train_rand, negatives, n_negatives=len(train_rand) * 2)\n",
    "val_rand_df = build_baseline_df(val_rand, negatives, n_negatives=len(val_rand) * 2)\n",
    "leaky_true, leaky_pred = train_and_predict(\"random\", train_rand_df, test_rand)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Training on pairwise split...\")\n",
    "clean_true, clean_pred = train_and_predict(\"pairwise\", train_df, test_df)\n",
    "\n",
    "impact = leakage_impact(leaky_true, leaky_pred, clean_true, clean_pred)\n",
    "print(json.dumps(impact, indent=2))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Save the calibrated model for the pipeline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "out_dir = settings.artifacts_path / \"deberta_v3_final\"\n",
    "model.save(out_dir)\n",
    "print(f\"Saved to {out_dir}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Quick smoke test\n",
    "from medguard.pipeline import MedGuardPipeline, PipelineConfig\n",
    "pipeline = MedGuardPipeline(config=PipelineConfig(use_model_predictions=True))\n",
    "pipeline.load_classifier(out_dir)\n",
    "result = pipeline.analyze_text(\"Tab Ecosprin AV 75mg, Tab Warfarin 5mg, Tab Metformin 500mg\")\n",
    "print(f\"Findings: {len(result.findings)}\")\n",
    "for f in result.findings:\n",
    "    print(f\"  {f.drug_a} + {f.drug_b} -> {f.severity.value} ({f.source}) conf={f.confidence.calibrated if f.confidence else 'N/A':.2f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Ablation: what did the normalisation buy us?\n",
    "\n",
    "Re-train without the brand→generic resolution (use raw surface forms as\n",
    "features). The F1 drop on the *real* corpus is the value of your alias\n",
    "table."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
